<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Arbanon</h1><p class="st-meta">1190 CE – 1255 CE (approx.) · capital Krujë</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Albanian state, a principality around Krujë ruled by the Progon family under Byzantine, Serbian and Epirote overlords.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Arbanon, in the mountains around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, gained autonomy in the late 12th century as Byzantine power declined. Its first known ruler was the archon Progon, around 1190, followed by his sons Gjin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhimiter-progoni">Dhimitër</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The archons ruled a Catholic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Albanian population from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a>, balancing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhimiter-progoni">Dhimitër Progoni</a>, who styled himself panhypersebastos, married Komnena, daughter of the Serbian ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-the-first-crowned">Stefan the First-Crowned</a>, and corresponded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a>. After his death around 1215, the Greek lord Gregory Kamonas and then Golem ruled.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From the 1230s Arbanon fell under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-epirus">Despotate of Epirus</a> and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/empire-of-nicaea">Empire of Nicaea</a>, which took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> around 1255. The area later formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-albania-medieval">Kingdom of Albania (medieval)</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-arbanon.jpg" alt="Principality of Arbanon" width="320" height="610"><figcaption>Image: Ahmet Q. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Arbanon_(Arb%C3%ABria).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1190 CE – 1255 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Krujë</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Progon, Dhimitër Progoni, Golem</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity (Catholic and Orthodox)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian; Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arbanon, Arbër</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1222&amp;focus=principality-of-arbanon" aria-label="Principality of Arbanon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5163 698 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Arbanon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5483 954L5709 970M5483 954L5519 1030M5483 954L5730 989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5519 1030h0M5730 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5483 954h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5483 954h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Krujë. <a href="/atlas?year=1222&amp;focus=principality-of-arbanon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

